</div>
</sideBySide>



<aside startOpen="true"><title>Stability theorem</title>


<p>We can summarize the results for the stability of discrete dynamical systems with the following stability theorem.</p>

<p>Consider the discrete dynamical system
<md>
  <mrow>x_{n+1}\amp = f(x_n)</mrow>
  <mrow>x_0\amp = a,</mrow>
</md>
with an 
<ref to="doenet:equilibria_discrete_dynamical_systems">equilibrium</ref><footnote>Recall that the fact that <m>E</m> is an equilibrium simply means that <m>E = f(E)</m>.
</footnote>
  <m>x_n = E</m>. Then, we can determine the stability of the equilibrium by calculating the derivative of <m>f</m> evaluated at the equilbrium as follows.</p>
<ul>
<li>If <m>|f'(E)| \lt  1</m>, then the equilibrium <m>x_n=E</m> is stable.</li>
<li>If <m>|f'(E)| \gt  1</m>, then the equilibrium <m>x_n = E</m> is unstable.</li>
<li>If <m>|f'(E)|=1</m>, then we can't figure out the stability of the equilibrium from just the derivative <m>f'(E)</m>.</li>
</ul>
</aside>

<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Explore the cobwebbing applet below for the given updating function.</p>

<p>
<booleanInput name="showDiagonal" prefill="true">
  <label>Show Cobwebbing and Diagonal line given by: <m>x_{n+1} = x_n</m></label>
</booleanInput></p>
<p>Enter updating function: <m>f(x) = </m> <mathInput prefill="1/8(x+3)(x-2)" name="formula" /></p>
<!-- <p>Sample evolution rule: <m>f(x) = </m> <math name="formula">0.05(x&#x2D;2)^3+1</math></p> -->

  <setup>
    <function name="f" symbolic="true">$formula</function>
    <solveEquations variables="x" name="solveForE" minVar="$xmin" maxVar="$xmax">$formula = x</solveEquations>
    <math extend="$A.x" name="px" />
    <derivative name="df">$f</derivative>
    <number name="num">10</number>
    <number name="zeroFixed" fixed="true">0</number>
    <point x="-8" y="$initialPoint.x" name="initialPoint" labelPosition="left">
<!--       <constraints baseOnGraph="g"> -->
      
        <constrainToGraph />
      
      <label>Initial Point</label>
    </point>
    
  </setup>
<!-- <asList>$solveForE.solutions</asList> -->


  <updateValue name="addLine" target="$num" newValue="$num+1" type="number">
    <label>Add line</label>
  </updateValue>
  <updateValue name="deleteLine" target="$num" newValue="max(1,$num-1)" type="number" disabled="$num &lt;= 1">
    <label>Delete line</label>
  </updateValue>

  <graph identicalAxisScales="true" grid="true" showNavigation="true" name="g">
  <xLabel><m>x_n</m></xLabel>
  <yLabel><m>x_{n+1}</m></yLabel>
  <point name="A" x="0" y="0" styleNumber="2">
    
      <repeat for="$solveForE.solutions" valueName="v"><attractTo><point>($v, $v)</point></attractTo></repeat>
      <constrainTo>$f</constrainTo>
      <constrainToGraph />
    
  </point>
      <line equation="y=$$df($px)(x-$px) + $$f($px)" fixed="true" styleNumber="3" name="tangentLine" />

    <function extend="$f" layer="1" styleNumber="2" />
    <cobwebPolyline function="$f" numPoints="$num" name="cobwebPolyline" initialPoint="$initialPoint" lockToSolution="true" draggable="false" hide="!$showDiagonal" />
    <point extend="$initialPoint" layer="2" />


    <point name="E1" styleNumber="5">($solveForE.solution1, $solveForE.solution1)
      <label><m>E_1</m></label>
    </point>
    <point name="E2" styleNumber="5">($solveForE.solution2, $solveForE.solution2)
      <label><m>E_2</m></label>
    </point>
    <point name="E3" styleNumber="5">($solveForE.solution3, $solveForE.solution3)
      <label><m>E_3</m></label>
    </point>
    
</graph>
<p>Use the <alert>word bank</alert> below to complete the summary of the equilibrium points of <m>f</m>:</p>
<p>The <textInput name="ti_1" /> point <m>E_1</m> is <textInput name="ti_2" />. This can be determined either by cobwebbing around the point <m>E_1</m> and observing that the values tend towards the point, or by observing that the <textInput name="ti_3" /> of the slope of the  <textInput name="ti_4" /> to <m>f</m> at point <m>E_1</m> is less than 1.</p>
<p>The equilibrium point at <m>E_2</m> is <textInput name="ti_5" />. Cobwebbing values near <m>E_2</m> tend <textInput name="ti_6" /> the point, and the <textInput name="ti_7" /> of <m>f</m> at point <m>E_2</m> is greater than 1.</p>
<answer name="ans1a" matchPartial="true" type="text">
  <award>
    <when>$ti_1 = equilibrium and $ti_2 = stable and $ti_3 = absolute value and $ti_4 = tangent line and $ti_5 = unstable and $ti_6 = away from and $ti_7 = derivative</when>
  </award>
</answer>
<p><alert>Word bank</alert></p>
  <tabular>
   <row>
     <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$absoluteValueUsed">
        <label>absolute value</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
      <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$stableUsed">
        <label>stable</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
      <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$derivativeUsed">
        <label>derivative</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
  </row>
  
  <row>
      <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$unstableUsed">
        <label>unstable</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
      <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$equilibriumUsed">
        <label>equilibrium</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
      <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$awayFromUsed">
        <label>away from</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
  </row>
  <row>
    <cell>
      <booleanInput prefill="$tangentLineUsed">
        <label>tangent line</label>
      </booleanInput></cell>
      <cell />
      <cell />
  </row>
  </tabular>


<setup>
<boolean name="absoluteValueUsed">$ti_1 = absolute value or $ti_2 = absolute value or $ti_3 = absolute value or $ti_4 = absolute value or $ti_5 = absolute value or $ti_6 = absolute value or $ti_7 = absolute value</boolean>

<boolean name="stableUsed">$ti_1 = stable or $ti_2 = stable or $ti_3 = stable or $ti_4 = stable or $ti_5 = stable or $ti_6 = stable or $ti_7 = stable</boolean>

<boolean name="derivativeUsed">$ti_1 = derivative or $ti_2 = derivative or $ti_3 = derivative or $ti_4 = derivative or $ti_5 = derivative or $ti_6 = derivative or $ti_7 = derivative</boolean>
  
<boolean name="unstableUsed">$ti_1 = unstable or $ti_2 = unstable or $ti_3 = unstable or $ti_4 = unstable or $ti_5 = unstable or $ti_6 = unstable or $ti_7 = unstable</boolean>

<boolean name="equilibriumUsed">$ti_1 = equilibrium or $ti_2 = equilibrium or $ti_3 = equilibrium or $ti_4 = equilibrium or $ti_5 = equilibrium or $ti_6 = equilibrium or $ti_7 = equilibrium</boolean>

<boolean name="awayFromUsed">$ti_1 = away from or $ti_2 = away from or $ti_3 = away from or $ti_4 = away from or $ti_5 = away from or $ti_6 = away from or $ti_7 = away from</boolean>

<boolean name="tangentLineUsed">$ti_1 = tangent line or $ti_2 = tangent line or $ti_3 = tangent line or $ti_4 = tangent line or $ti_5 = tangent line or $ti_6 = tangent line or $ti_7 = tangent line</boolean>

</setup>
</exercise>
</problem>
  
</section>
